---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import { APP } from '../consts';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../lib/schema';

const trail = [{ label: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy/' }];
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Plantive"
  description="How Plantive handles your data, including the photos you take for plant identification. Read the full privacy policy for Plantive by DEDUCTIFY, LLC."
  canonical="/privacy/"
  schema={[breadcrumbs(trail)]}
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-prose page">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={trail} />
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The full privacy policy for {APP.name} is maintained as a published document by {APP.developer}.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={APP.privacyUrl} rel="noopener" target="_blank">
        Read the full privacy policy →
      </a>
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>In short</h2>
      <p>
        Plantive processes the photos you take in order to identify the plant in them. What is
        collected, how long it is kept, who it is shared with and the rights you have over it are all
        set out in the policy linked above, which is the authoritative version.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        The plant care guides on plantiveapp.com are free to read. The site loads Ahrefs Web
        Analytics to count visits. When the site owner explicitly enables it in the production
        configuration, Google Analytics also measures page views and App Store link clicks. The
        website sends the page path, content group and button location with that custom click event;
        it does not add form entries or arbitrary query parameters.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is no advertising or ad-network code on this site. Browser privacy controls and
        extensions may block analytics requests.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        For any privacy question, or to make a request about your data, email
        <EmailLink />.
      </p>
      <p>
        See also our <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a> and <a href="/support/">support page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-top: 2.25rem;
  }

  .page h1 {
    margin-block: 1rem 0.9rem;
  }

  .page .lede {
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .page .btn {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
